    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Founded around 1465 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerei-khan">Kerei</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janibek-khan">Janibek</a>, who broke away from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-khayr-khan">Abu'l-Khayr Khan</a> with their followers.</li><li>A nomadic confederation of three juzes under Genghisid khans, with law kept by biys and codified in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhety-zhargy">Zhety Zhargy</a>.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungar</a> invasions after 1723 drove the juzes towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, which abolished the khans' power in the 1820s.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazakhs">Kazakh</a> is generally explained as meaning a free or independent wanderer, a word once used of men who had broken away from their own tribe or ruler.</p></aside>
    </section>

